riginal red TRX reproduces these effects, rather than merely checking a reason code.', 'id': 'PATH-STRUCTURAL-LOOP-ENTRY-1', 'limits': 'The five fake-boundary cases prove wrong-resource selection and fresh submission identity. The actual WPF condition flow proves shared primary entry and real round waiting; it does not prove resource/game effects or every unrelated explicit-entry permutation.', 'obligation': 'implementation', 'paths': ['source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/ViewModels/WorkflowScheduleViewModel.cs:67', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowPlanner.cs:88', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowPlanner.cs:90', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowPlanner.cs:95', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowPlan.Path.cs:97', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowPlan.Path.cs:118', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:743', 'source/Test/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant.UnitTest/ServiceTests/TaskCenter/PathLoopCutoffTests.cs:15'], 'repair_steps': ['Completed: FirstOccurrence and both structural restart branches use StructuralRoundEntry, preserving the primary entry and PathLane=0.', \"Completed: Runner binds round-start waiting to IsStructuralRoundEntry's stable node/occurrence identity.\", 'Completed: Structural restart increments durable LoopIteration; explicitly selected back edges retain their existing target/lane semantics.', 'Completed: No lane quota, daily deduplication or scan of unselected branches was introduced.'], 'root_cause': 'The prior structural restarts used array position zero while first entry selected the first node covering primary lane zero. Formal scheduling globally sorts all lanes by time, so the earlier secondary node could occupy position zero. Runner round scheduling also used SequenceIndex==0 rather than that canonical entry.', 'severity': 'important', 'status': 'resolved_with_evidence', 'tests': [{'case': 'StructuralLoop_RestartsPrimaryEntryAfterEarlierSecondaryNode(explicitEnd: True)', 'test_id': 'cbc65cd2-3741-cb57-df1d-5087715a15fd'}, {'case': 'StructuralLoop_RestartsPrimaryEntryAfterEarlierSecondaryNode(explicitEnd: False)', 'test_id': '9a7d16ef-05a4-ea04-4381-422b8551b41b'}, {'case': 'StructuralLoop_TwoRoundsSubmitOnlySelectedPrimaryWithFreshIdentity(explicitEnd: True)', 'test_id': 'c8a95ff4-2aaa-a9d4-e33d-3262d847e05a'}, {'case': 'StructuralLoop_TwoRoundsSubmitOnlySelectedPrimaryWithFreshIdentity(explicitEnd: False)', 'test_id': 'e6ed5485-3fa8-975d-99ba-7cdecb1bbc59'}, {'case': 'ScheduledLoop_NonzeroPrimaryEntryStillWaitsForNextRound', 'test_id': '44de1881-ef12-d159-5469-941dcc230fad'}]}, {'closure_evidence': ['PC/red/path-cutoff.trx: four absolute-deadline cases fail with prerequisite Expected 0/Actual 1; the old scheduled-round case fails because late was submitted at 11:00. The already-started positive case passes.', 'PC/green/path-cutoff.trx and both restored affected regressions: all six cases pass.', 'PC/negative-cutoff/path-cutoff.trx: removing the post-wait absolute deadline guard and node-wait cutoff cap makes four zero-prerequisite assertions fail with Actual 1. The scheduled-round test fails on waiting 2 hours instead of the expected 1 hour; its post-wait expiry guard remains active, so that mutant is not claimed to prove its independent absence.', 'PC/negative-cutoff-source-restored.json and independent comparison: both production files equal the saved original bytes and current frozen source.', 'PC/product-actual/fixtures-retimed/wf-own-cutoff-01a1176e.flow.json: node lower bound 02:23, loop cutoff 02:22, revision b32908d9272bb101368beaba593a0795d2456c2a3cb19d1f51d3f19fea91c580.', 'PC/product-actual/private/native-ui-source.jsonl line 118: actual WPF card shows waiting to 02:22.', 'PC/product-actual/actual-terminal-runs/run-3816f2d66d58.run.json: updated at 02:22:00.0558554+08:00, Succeeded, TailReached=true, Wait=null, StopRequested=false, no node outcomes/prerequisites/submission history, bound original deadline and terminal seal.', 'Affected regression includes original deadline/LocalWait/stop/pause/terminal/explicit-back-edge cases and retains exactly the original two unrelated LocalWait failures.'], 'counterexample': 'A 09:00 run with deadline 10:00 and a sequence/fixed resource at 11:00 previously invoked its prerequisite after the cutoff. A flexible node becoming idle only after cutoff also invoked it. The original expired scheduled-round case submitted late at 11:00 instead of skipping the old round.', 'id': 'LOOP-CUTOFF-TIMED-NODE-1', 'limits': 'This closes the supported timed-node waiting gap and bounded expiry behavior. The finite fake-boundary tests prove zero prerequisite/body-send calls; actual WPF observations prove shared wait/arrival settlement without resources. No gameplay acceptance, arbitrary timing stress or separate causal proof of every guard is claimed.', 'obligation': 'implementation', 'paths': ['source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:739', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:772', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:775', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:776', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:1627', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:1648', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowRunner.cs:1668', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowNodeSchedule.cs:99', 'source/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant/Services/TaskCenter/WorkflowNodeSchedule.cs:117', 'source/Test/MultiplayerHoeingAssistant.UnitTest/ServiceTests/TaskCenter/PathLoopCutoffTests.cs:74'], 'repair_steps': ['Completed: cap node waits at the earlier absolute loop deadline or applicable durable scheduled-round end.', 'Completed: sequence/fixed/fle